# Automations & Integrations

## Scheduling

**Production:** Supabase **`pg_cron` + `pg_net`** (every minute) → `GET /api/cron/dispatch` with `CRON_SECRET` from Vault. See **`docs/temp/scheduled-jobs-and-testing.md`**. Vercel Hobby cannot use sub-daily `vercel.json` crons. The dispatcher runs due `automation_jobs` (per user timezone): `send_due_reminders` (default seeded daily 12:00 PM) and user-created `run_soa_pipeline` jobs—not macOS launchd.

| Job type | Legacy CLI | KameOps |
| -------- | ---------- | ------- |
| SOA pipeline | `npm run start` / manual month | `run_soa_pipeline` automation or **Run SOA** UI |
| Due reminders | `send-reminders` (launchd) | Default `send_due_reminders` automation; edit schedule on **Automations**; window/interval on **Credit Cards** |
| Telegram bot | long-polling daemon | **Webhook** at `/api/webhooks/telegram` |

Cron routes must verify `CRON_SECRET`. Log every run to `automation_runs`.

## Integrations Model

Store per user in `integrations` table:

| Provider | Capabilities |
| -------- | ------------ |
| `gmail` | SOA fetch (Run SOA Gmail search) |
| `google_calendar` | Due-date events, mark paid |
| `telegram` | Bot token, chat id, web link |
| `slack` | Incoming webhook URL |

Use service abstractions—routers and UI never call Telegram/Slack APIs directly. Outbound messages go through `notification.service.ts`.

## Idempotency

Reminder send fingerprints live in `reminder_logs` (Postgres idempotency).

## Telegram Webhook

- Replace long-polling `telegram-bot-listener.ts` with webhook handler
- Handle: paid/unpaid text, receipt photos, optional startup message
- Verify webhook secret / bot token on each request

## Environment vs Database

| Legacy | KameOps |
| ------ | ------- |
| Global `.env` tokens | Per-user integration records |
| `GEMINI_*`, `GROQ_*` env | Settings → `ai_api_keys` (encrypted, per user) |
| `CARDS_JSON` | `credit_cards` table |
| `data/*.json` state | Postgres tables |

Keep `.env` only for app secrets (Supabase, cron secret)—not user card passwords or receipt AI keys.

## Failure Handling

- Automation run failures: persist `errorMessage` on failed SOA runs
- Integration disconnect: surface UI banner + disable dependent jobs
- Rate limits: backoff and log; never silent fail reminders
